<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- No android:packageNames: the four built-in feeds plus any user-added apps must all
     wake the service. The code filters events against Prefs.trackedApps (an in-memory
     read) before counting a pixel, so untracked apps cost one string compare each.

     canRetrieveWindowContent is deliberately still absent. Nothing here reads a single
     node, label or piece of text — only the scroll numbers the event itself carries — so
     the privacy claim in the README stands exactly as written.

     notificationTimeout="0", not 50: the system keeps at most ONE pending event per event
     type per service inside that window and recycles the rest
     (AbstractAccessibilityServiceConnection.notifyAccessibilityEvent). Every dropped
     TYPE_VIEW_SCROLLED is a scroll delta we never get told about again, and an app with
     two scrollers on screen loses whichever one reported first. A counter cannot afford
     the coalescing a screen reader wants.

     flagIncludeNotImportantViews: wantsEventLocked() silently discards every event whose
     source view isn't important for accessibility unless the service asks for those too.
     Feeds that draw their own custom containers land on the wrong side of that check, and
     they lose the whole event, not just its fields. The flag only widens which events and
     nodes may be delivered; it grants no content access on its own.

     typeWindowStateChanged is low-volume and buys two things: baselines for the scroll
     position diff are dropped when the foreground app changes (a position from another
     app's feed is worse than no position), and the diagnostics can tell "we never heard
     from YouTube" apart from "we heard from YouTube and it told us nothing". -->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeViewScrolled|typeWindowStateChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagIncludeNotImportantViews"
    android:notificationTimeout="0"
    android:description="@string/service_description" />
